+# Race subpage response, 2026-10-23
+
+The owner reports that Race subpages fall behind presses. RMI01 responds to rail buttons on press. RMI02 retains one actual Weekly Rivalry page between visits. RMI03 preserves vertical ordering, fixed navigation, first-entry data readiness, updated status, account/car/server/population scope and ordinary primary-page gestures. R01/Q01 cover isolated regression checks and a task-only review patch.
+
+The temporary race-mode rail disappears when the 0.32-second slide ends. Its original release-triggered button could disappear between mouse DOWN and UP, silently losing the selection. Rail buttons now activate on DOWN through Godot's native action mode. These stationary navigation buttons own their touches, while content keeps its existing scroll and swipe ownership. The slide, ordering and appearance remain the same.
+
+Returning to Rivalry also rebuilt three native podium cars. The App now parks at most one actual Rivalry page after its departing slide completes. The hidden parent disables processing/input and explicitly stops its subviewports. Reentry updates the existing presentation before attaching it, restoring the visible rail; scope changes discard the cached page. Existing score/status refreshes, explicit overview entry, standings offsets, first-response gating, menu suspension, race results and shutdown remain under the original owners. Cold first construction and real network waits remain.
+
+Changed runtime files: `game/ui/race_mode_rail.gd`, `game/core/app.gd`. Regression: `game/tests/test_race_mode_input.gd` and UID. The original-source swipe reproducer is `game/tests/fixtures/race_mode_input_before/test_menu_page_swipe_before.gd`; it loads the saved task-original App rather than changing live source. Evidence, receipts, fingerprints and scoped patch are in [the report](evidence/race-mode-input-2026-10-23/report.json).
+
+All Godot commands use `powershell -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File scripts/dev.ps1`, the pinned `4.7.2.stable.official.ed1daf0bf` engine, workspace-isolated `APPDATA` and disabled backend access. Exact arguments and outcomes are recorded in the report. Native captures use `-Graphical -RenderingMethod gl_compatibility` or `mobile`; desktop Mobile is not an Android-device result.
+
+The original input probe produced **16 failures in 34 checks**, including two lost mouse selections at slide completion. The press-only fix passed all 34. Retention's initial 47-check probe caught two viewports left armed while hidden; explicit viewport disabling corrected that defect without removing the assertions. The final probe also covers rapid alternating real touch input, retained page/car identity, no reconstruction, hidden inactivity, current parked status, rail visibility, cache bounds and account-scope replacement.
+
+In a paired local headless fixture, repeated Rivalry dispatch after the press fix but before retention took **404.026–486.345 ms**. Retention reduced the same four dispatches to **21.417–34.562 ms**. These are synchronous input-handler measurements with explicit UI fixture data, not first-presented-frame, phone FPS, network or memory certification. Both renderers also record their own timings in `input.json`.
+
+Native views: [reused Rivalry in Compatibility](evidence/race-mode-input-2026-10-23/final-gl_compatibility/reused-rivalry-960x540.png), [reused Rivalry in desktop Mobile](evidence/race-mode-input-2026-10-23/final-mobile/reused-rivalry-960x540.png), and [Free Race after rapid presses](evidence/race-mode-input-2026-10-23/final-mobile/free-race-960x540.png). The empty offline Free Race catalogue and Rivalry concept standings are isolated fixtures, not live accounts or scores.
+
+Final input checks pass **57 headless / 62 Compatibility / 62 desktop Mobile**, including screenshots. Existing carousel **42**, delayed entry **66**, standings stability **44**, Weekly Rivalry **1115**, App **141** and parser **979** pass. Parser count reflects concurrent source additions at the time of the run.
+
+The broad `test_menu_page_swipe.gd` run reports three live-drag failures and then a nil tween pause error. Its task-original App reproducer reports the same three failures and error. The broad menu-medium suite passes its retained Rivalry checks but reports 30 washing assertions; the task-original App reproduces all 30. Its result and original-App comparison are retained separately. Assertions remain unchanged, and neither broad suite is claimed as passing. Initial local launcher attempts also hit PowerShell execution policy, then the restricted user directory/root-certificate store; successful runs use the documented launcher, isolated storage and approved certificate-store access.
+
+Physical-device touch/latency, owner feel and long-session memory acceptance remain. No phone attachment check or physical-device test, APK build/install, live backend/account mutation, sharing or deployment was performed.
